---
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/render-loop-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/render-loop-dark.svg?raw';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={620}
  caption="The loop that built the collar: five shapes in an evening, each one a sentence, judged at the render and priced at the slicer."
>
  A one-line ask goes to Claude, which edits the OpenSCAD source. OpenSCAD
  renders the part to a PNG. I eyeball the render and sometimes slice it. If
  it is not right yet, the loop returns to another one-line ask; when it holds
  up, the part prints in ASA.
</Diagram>
